nodecode-boxcompute is a rewrite of boxcompute's boxcompute/hermes-plugin:

  https://github.com/boxcompute/hermes-plugin
  commit de27f5719372905686474f8a7650c591c63e899c
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 BoxCompute (LICENSE)

The original carried no code: a portable manifest (plugin.json), one skill
(skills/sandboxes/SKILL.md), a banner, and a line the user ran by hand,
`hermes mcp add boxcompute --url https://mcp.boxcompute.ai/mcp --auth oauth`,
which added BoxCompute's hosted MCP server to Hermes and let Hermes discover
its tools. The server is still the service here, and the skill is still the
guidance, but this cell is the MCP client itself: wire.lisp speaks JSON-RPC
over streamable HTTP with nlk:http, keep the session id the initialize answer
issues, and call tools/call; tools.lisp declares six tools over the server's
own; and +PRIMER+, the skill's rules (when to use a VM instead of the user's
machine, start small, run long work as a process, stop to stop paying, a
preview link is public, delete only when asked), is (help :boxcompute).
What was left out: the OAuth sign-in and the browser flow (a cell's section
is one key, and Hermes owned the token store, so an API key is the way in
here), the manifest's tool discovery at connect time (the six tools declare
their arguments, and boxcompute:tools, boxcompute:schema read the server's
catalog live for anything else), and the banner. Nothing of the original is
vendored.
